export anchor StarChartStyle:
    number: 129
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Star chart
    idea: A pale celestial chart where projects are stars plotted on a dotted coordinate grid and joined by a constellation line, numbers are magnitudes in an oval cartouche and the daily chart is a light curve.
    base: light
    palette:
        skyPaper: #eef1f8, the page, with a #cfd5ea dot field
        chartField: #fbfcff, panels and fields
        nightNavy: #1b2550, text, stars, borders and the On track star
        dusk: #46507a, axis labels and captions
        grid: #cdd3e6, dotted coordinate lines and the inner frame line
        constellation: #7584bf, lines joining stars, never text
        halo: #e3e8f7, soft discs behind stars and the avatar
        brass: #7f5a00, the week divider and week totals
        atRisk: #7a3e8c, the diamond
        behind: #a2262e, the crossed circle and overdue
        focus: #3953c9, the 2px focus ring
    type:
        One stack, Optima, Candara, Segoe UI, Noto Sans, Seravek, sans-serif.
        The greeting is 46px 400 at 1.1, magnitudes 34px 400, panel titles
        22px 400 tracked 0.06em, Greek star letters 18px bold italic, body
        16px at 1.5, labels and the date 12 to 13px caps tracked 0.18 to
        0.3em.
    layout:
        A header ruled underneath with a compass star logo, the spaced caps
        brand, nav links in small spaced caps each led by a dot, Home led by
        a small filled star, then a pill search, a navy pill New project
        button, a round bell and a round avatar with the name. The intro has
        the light greeting, the spaced caps date and a crossed circle line
        saying 4 tasks are overdue, and on the right an oval cartouche with
        a double line border titled Magnitudes this week, holding the four
        numbers each beside a navy dot sized by its value, overdue as an open
        red ring. The main panel, The project sky, has an engraved double
        border and plots the six projects on a dotted grid, due date across
        from 1 Nov to 15 Jan and percent complete up, each a navy mark on a
        halo disc sized by task count, its shape showing status, labelled
        with its Greek letter, name and percent, all joined in due date order
        by a thin constellation line. Below, a Catalogue table lists Greek
        letter, project, team, percent, tasks, due date and status, beside
        an Observation log with the time in spaced caps. A wide Light curve
        panel plots the 14 days as dots sized by value on a thin line, with
        a brass dashed divider and week totals. Below 1060px the cartouche
        and panels stack, below 640px both charts scroll sideways inside
        their panels.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 24px between panels, 20 to 24px panel padding, a 24px dot field behind.
    density: Airy. One wide sky chart, then catalogue and log side by side, then the light curve.
    corners: Fully round search, buttons and fields, a 120px oval cartouche and 6px panels.
    borders: A 1px navy outer line with a 1px grid blue inner line 5px inside, like an engraved map border.
    shadows: None. Stars sit on soft halo discs instead.
    icons:
        Celestial marks at 16px with the word, a five point star for On
        track, a diamond for At risk and a crossed circle for Behind. In the
        sky the same shapes are drawn larger, sized by task count.
    focus: A 2px blue outline offset 3px with a 6px soft blue halo.
    tone: Calm observatory words, such as Magnitudes this week, Catalogue, Observation log and Light curve.
